WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.160
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:08.960
By the way!  Flame, you know what 
happened to Cyberse World, right?

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:14.020
We held many discussions 
after you hid Cyberse World.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:19.760
We discussed whether to trust humans and 
give our technology so we can live together.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:24.140
That's when a new enemy attacked.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:29.320
We barely escaped Cyberse World alive.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:33.210
Windy, we're after someone.

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:35.320
His name is Bohman.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:38.280
He stole my acquaintance's 
brother's consciousness data.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:43.660
He had the same card as the one 
who destroyed Cyberse World.

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:48.410
That's very interesting.  But I don't know.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:51.000
Will you help us?

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:59.140
Instead of helping humans, we can rebuild 
Cyberse World quicker if the Ignis come together.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:04.250
It's true that the Ignis wish 
to rebuild Cyberse World.

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:06.370
But I'll pursue the culprit.

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:10.250
I want to know the truth about 
Cyberse World's destruction.

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:33.320
Our lives aren't forever

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:40.110
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:47.430
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:54.010
Sharing hope for the future

00:01:54.010 --> 00:02:00.750
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:07.990
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:14.690
I want to share your pain

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:50.570
Our master has a lot of 
fan posts again today.

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:54.290
Let me see…

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:56.160
"Playmaker is cool!"

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:01.010
"The last duel was godly."

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:05.140
"The Cyberse Deck is the strongest."

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:09.090
They don’t know anything!

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:15.340
“Playmaker is strong because 
he has a talented AI named Ai.”

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:18.060
Tooting your own horn!  As usual!

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:19.960
What do you mean, “As usual?”

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:22.500
You make it sound like I always do this!

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:24.080
But you are!

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:29.140
You've posted 212 times 
on this message board.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:31.300
Be quiet!

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:35.530
I’m just letting everyone know the truth!

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:39.370
Since you're stuck in this 
room, you don't know this:

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:44.440
But in the other world, the master 
can’t do anything without me-

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:45.850
Who're you talking about?

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:50.780
Master, he was pretending to be-

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:53.200
Hey!  It’s a new message.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.730
Playmaker, you’re so popular!

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:57.850
It says…

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:00.200
"Mr. Earth Ignis"

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:03.880
Whaaaaaat?

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:07.860
"I want to meet Playmaker."

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:12.400
This post is from the Earth Ignis?

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:16.800
It's obviously a hoax.

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:19.290
We don't know for sure.

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:23.400
Only a few know about the Ignis’ existence.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:29.020
Even if that’s true, would an 
Ignis post on a message board?

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:32.020
The Earth Ignis would.

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:34.260
So he’s alive.

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:37.980
And that Ignis wants to meet Yusaku?

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:40.960
He’s a straight shooter.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:43.970
He may want to tell us something.

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:47.340
Maybe he knows something about Bohman.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.080
Can you contact him?

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:51.320
Leave it to me!

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:56.300
If you find any info related to 
the Ignis, report immediately!

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:57.140
Yes sir!

00:04:57.140 --> 00:04:59.730
The higher-ups asked for 
me.  You're in charge.

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:02.040
Okay!  Understood!

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:10.020
At first glance, it looks like garbled text.

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:14.000
But I used an Ignis algorithm 
to ask where to meet.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.800
Only an Ignis can read this.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:19.500
Let’s see if we get a nibble.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:24.220
A response!

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:27.700
See?  Just like I said.

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:29.220
What does it say?

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:32.680
They're coordinates.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:34.700
So we have to go there.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:39.100
But we still don’t know 
if it’s the real Ignis.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:42.210
It might be Blood Shepherd's trap again.

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:46.500
Because he knows the Ignis algorithm.

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:50.610
C’mon, Kusanagi.  You’re so suspicious.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:54.530
Even if it’s a risk, we need info.

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:58.610
To retrieve your brother’s 
consciousness data.

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:00.180
Yusaku…

00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:03.180
So let's hurry.

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:06.850
SOL Technologies must've seen this post too.

00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:08.560
Thanks, Yusaku.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:14.690
What is it?

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:18.930
While gathering info on 
Playmaker, I found this.

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:20.780
This is…

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:28.260
You're struggling mightily 
to capture the Ignis.

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:31.130
We're continuing to search at full strength.

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:36.220
Your bounty hunters haven’t 
achieved any results either.

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:37.580
I apologize.

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:40.330
How's that certain mission going?

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:43.580
As you ordered, Go Onizuka is undertaking it.

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:46.560
The program should end soon.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:50.810
Fine.  But take this to heart.

00:06:51.290 --> 00:06:57.050
My company isn’t so generous that we'd 
keep employees who don’t achieve results.

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:12.640
These are the Ignis's coordinates.

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:14.340
Be careful.

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:18.730
SOL Technologies' people 
may be hiding around here.

00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:22.020
Like Onizuka or that gunman.

00:07:28.230 --> 00:07:30.980
"Mr. Earth Ignis?"

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:32.640
Earth Ignis?

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:34.580
“I want to meet Playmaker.”

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:35.530
What is this?

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:38.180
Umm…

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:44.490
There’s no way a real Ignis would post 
as an Ignis on an anonymous message board.

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:46.410
It's definitely a hoax.

00:07:46.410 --> 00:07:48.650
Well?  Anything?

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:51.620
Nothing in particular.

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:56.860
There’s a total of six Ignis, right?

00:07:56.860 --> 00:07:57.920
Yeah.

00:07:57.920 --> 00:08:00.400
Flame, Windy and you.

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:02.850
What are the other three Ignis like?

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:05.200
Well…

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:07.770
First, the Light Ignis.

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:10.670
Calm, cool and collected.  Like a leader.

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:17.880
But too smart.  So I can’t understand 
what it's thinking at all.

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:21.210
Next is the subleader, the Water Ignis.

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:24.480
Has the skill to tell the difference 
between lies and truth.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:28.360
That’s why Cyberse World never 
had betrayals or conspiracies.

00:08:28.930 --> 00:08:33.340
It’s embarrassing for me to say...

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:37.570
...but the Water Ignis super relied on me.

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:42.110
The Water Ignis definitely liked me.

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:48.310
I see.

00:08:48.310 --> 00:08:50.580
Huh?  That's it for a reaction?

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:55.030
The others are Flame.  And 
the Wind Ignis, Windy.

00:08:55.030 --> 00:09:00.340
And…  Oh, the Earth Ignis.

00:09:00.340 --> 00:09:05.170
He’s no-nonsense and honest and umm…

00:09:05.170 --> 00:09:06.450
Oh!

00:09:06.450 --> 00:09:09.170
He's like this guy, massive and orange!

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:11.760
It's the Earth Ignis!

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:14.300
Long time, no see!  How have you been?

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:16.000
You’re the Earth Ignis?

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:17.910
Yeah, this guy!

00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:21.520
This way.  Follow me.

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:24.530
What’s with him?

00:09:24.530 --> 00:09:26.460
Let’s celebrate our reunion more!

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:27.250
Let’s go.

00:09:34.150 --> 00:09:35.960
Wait up, Earth!

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:40.070
"Earth?"  Do you mean me?

00:09:40.070 --> 00:09:43.440
Yeah.  I just named you.

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:47.120
Because humans can’t 
pronounce our real names.

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:49.300
By the way, they call me Ai.

00:09:49.300 --> 00:09:54.550
Don't tell me you're named 
Ai because you’re an AI?

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:56.720
Of course not, dummy.

00:09:56.720 --> 00:10:00.010
I see.  It’s a good, logical name.

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:04.790
Right?  I knew you’d understand!

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:07.520
What do you want with me?

00:10:09.490 --> 00:10:14.350
Well?  You called us for a reason, right?

00:10:14.350 --> 00:10:16.240
C'mon, say something.

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:21.210
Duel me, Playmaker.

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:31.360
Duel you?

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:32.420
Yes.

00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:35.410
Is it because you don’t 
like the name Earth?

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:37.500
This is too sudden!

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:40.050
I am socially awkward.

00:10:40.050 --> 00:10:41.650
It’s not about that!

00:10:41.650 --> 00:10:44.070
I don’t get why, so explain!

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:47.060
I see.  Fine.

00:10:48.140 --> 00:10:50.200
You’re unexpectedly understanding.

00:10:50.200 --> 00:10:52.410
Okay.  Please explain.

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:55.050
To determine the truth.

00:10:55.050 --> 00:11:01.650
To verify human’s true nature with 
my own eyes, I'll duel Playmaker.

00:11:02.110 --> 00:11:05.680
That’s not a good explanation!

00:11:06.510 --> 00:11:08.920
The Water Ignis…

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:14.630
What’s the Water Ignis’s 
name in the human world?

00:11:14.630 --> 00:11:20.950
Well…  Since it’s a 
Water Ignis, how about Wa-

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:24.110
Wait.  I’ll choose.

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:28.970
Aqua.

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:32.310
Yes, that’s a good name.  It's decided.

00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:36.370
Aqua said to me:

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:42.430
The Cyberse World will soon break apart.

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:47.300
Human or Ignis, which side will you join?

00:11:47.300 --> 00:11:49.490
Human or Ignis?

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:52.500
Verify with your own eyes.

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:57.920
What's the truth for 
humanity and AI’s future?

00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:00.970
What’s the truth…

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:04.200
Humanity and AI’s future…

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:07.570
The more I hear, the more I don’t get.

00:12:07.570 --> 00:12:10.360
Cyberse World will break apart?

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:12.720
Forget breaking apart!  It was destroyed!

00:12:12.970 --> 00:12:14.750
That’s not what I mean.

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:16.960
I’m talking about us Ignis.

00:12:18.060 --> 00:12:19.500
What are you talking about?

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:22.810
Ai, why did you join the human side?

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:26.670
Why are you with Playmaker?

00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:30.770
Why?  Because a passionate 
friendship unites us!

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:32.670
Right, Playmaker?

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:34.260
See?

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:38.150
I want to ask you something.

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:39.450
Ask me?

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:42.400
We’re searching for a man named Bohman.

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:46.380
He stole my acquaintance’s 
brother’s consciousness data.

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:51.390
And he seems to be linked to 
Cyberse World’s destruction.

00:12:51.390 --> 00:12:55.120
If you have any info about 
Bohman, please tell me.

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:59.870
If you want to ask for that info, duel me.

00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:03.600
I knew you’d say that.  So annoying.

00:13:03.980 --> 00:13:06.070
I am socially awkward.

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:10.010
You think that’s cool?

00:13:11.280 --> 00:13:12.540
Ignoring me?

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:14.820
Fine.  Let’s duel.

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:18.280
But Earth, how will you duel?

00:13:42.610 --> 00:13:44.370
Your partner is-

00:13:44.370 --> 00:13:46.610
Let’s fight, Playmaker!

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:50.050
Okay.  Let’s fight!

00:13:50.320 --> 00:13:52.020
Duel!

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:56.750
Earth!  C’mon, bring it on!

00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:10.900
You’re not going to bring it on?

00:14:11.260 --> 00:14:13.910
I choose to go second.

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:16.110
Then say that from the start!

00:14:16.110 --> 00:14:17.680
I am socially awkward.

00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:20.230
That’s not fair!

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:22.880
I am... socially awkward.

00:14:23.110 --> 00:14:25.590
Yeah yeah, I get it.

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:27.620
Then I’ll go first.

00:14:28.120 --> 00:14:31.360
I summon Poisoning Blocker from my hand!

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:36.820
Poisoning Blocker’s effect!

00:14:36.820 --> 00:14:41.060
Once per turn, it can change 
from attack to defense position!

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:47.300
When this effect is used, this 
monster gains 800 ATK and DEF!

00:14:47.300 --> 00:14:49.820
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:14:52.230 --> 00:14:55.680
A decent start, Playmaker.

00:14:57.650 --> 00:14:59.540
My turn.

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:03.400
Ai!  Humans destroyed Cyberse World!

00:15:04.190 --> 00:15:06.640
Still have something to say?

00:15:06.640 --> 00:15:07.670
Yes.

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:09.460
Make it quick.

00:15:09.460 --> 00:15:16.430
Only humans and us Ignis can build high 
level civilizations in this world.

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:19.900
And Ignis don't need to fight each other.

00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:23.600
That’s true.  So what?

00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:30.430
That means it’s natural to conclude 
that humans destroyed Cyberse World.

00:15:30.430 --> 00:15:32.620
That’s the logical answer.

00:15:33.980 --> 00:15:36.950
Like I said, it’s Bohman’s fault-

00:15:37.600 --> 00:15:41.630
Come to think of it, who is he?

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:46.790
So why do you still side with the humans?

00:15:46.790 --> 00:15:49.910
I'll learn why in this duel!

00:15:49.910 --> 00:15:51.030
I draw!

00:15:52.330 --> 00:15:57.170
His original partner is likely Spectre.

00:15:57.170 --> 00:16:00.820
Seriously?  Is that why he hates humans?

00:16:00.820 --> 00:16:03.020
Makes sense if it’s Spectre.

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:04.700
Have any data on him?

00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:06.650
What’s his dueling style?

00:16:06.650 --> 00:16:10.890
Umm…  I don’t remember.

00:16:11.310 --> 00:16:13.630
He never stood out.

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:18.860
From my hand, I activate 
the spell card, Cost Down.

00:16:20.920 --> 00:16:23.020
By discarding a card from my hand...

00:16:23.020 --> 00:16:27.510
...this turn, I lower the Level 
of a monster in my hand by 2.

00:16:27.510 --> 00:16:33.880
I lower G Golem Rock Hammer's 
Level from 6 to 4 and summon it!

00:16:35.450 --> 00:16:37.440
That looks tough.

00:16:37.440 --> 00:16:40.180
G Golem Rock Hammer’s effect!

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:48.420
By tributing it, I Special Summon three G 
Golem Tokens on my field in defense position.

00:16:48.850 --> 00:16:50.780
Three Tokens.

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:52.160
He’s going to Link Summon.

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:55.600
Appear!  The circuit that roars the land!

00:16:55.600 --> 00:16:59.740
The summoning conditions are 
at least two Earth monsters.

00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:04.250
I set three G Golem Tokens 
in the Link Markers!

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:05.470
Link Summon!

00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:14.750
Appear, Link 3 G Golem Invalid Dolmen!

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:24.260
Battle!  G Golem Invalid Dolmen 
attacks Poisoning Blocker!

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:37.700
When G Golem Invalid Dolmen attacks a monster 
in defense position, it deals piercing damage!

00:17:40.670 --> 00:17:42.880
I end my turn.

00:17:43.270 --> 00:17:45.200
Now I remember!

00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:45.880
What?

00:17:46.150 --> 00:17:48.880
Earth was great at dueling!

00:17:51.120 --> 00:17:55.620
I should've remembered that 
a bit earlier.  Oh well.

00:17:57.200 --> 00:17:59.510
My turn!  I draw!

00:17:59.830 --> 00:18:02.530
I summon Bitron from my hand!

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:08.500
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:13.210
The summoning condition is 
one Cyberse Normal Monster!

00:18:13.210 --> 00:18:16.190
I set Bitron in the Link Marker!

00:18:16.190 --> 00:18:17.660
Link Summon!

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:21.380
Appear!  Link 1 Zombie Prosaber!

00:18:23.630 --> 00:18:24.810
Battle!

00:18:24.810 --> 00:18:28.360
Zombie Prosaber attacks Invalid Dolmen!

00:18:28.810 --> 00:18:30.600
It has1600 ATK!

00:18:30.600 --> 00:18:32.840
And you attack a monster with 2800 ATK?

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:36.930
I activate the trap card, Link Rush!

00:18:36.930 --> 00:18:40.570
When a Link Summoned monster 
battles this turn...

00:18:40.570 --> 00:18:44.550
...your monster is destroyed 
without calculating damage!

00:18:50.780 --> 00:18:53.790
Zombie Prosaber’s effect activates!

00:18:54.120 --> 00:18:56.960
When a monster on your field that's next to its link

00:18:56.960 --> 00:18:59.240
is destroyed in battle or by an effect...

00:18:59.750 --> 00:19:05.270
...that monster is Special Summoned 
from your graveyard to my field!

00:19:05.270 --> 00:19:09.470
All right!  Steal his monster!

00:19:09.470 --> 00:19:11.080
I won’t let you!

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:13.810
G Golem Invalid Dolmen’s effect!

00:19:14.260 --> 00:19:22.370
When it's destroyed, it negates the 
effects of all your faceup cards.

00:19:27.430 --> 00:19:29.810
It negated my effect.

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:32.820
Too bad!  You couldn’t steal it!

00:19:32.820 --> 00:19:35.820
So what'll you try next?

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:38.720
I suggest attacking.

00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:39.670
Be quiet.

00:19:39.670 --> 00:19:42.940
But I know so much about Earth!

00:19:42.940 --> 00:19:45.880
You just said you didn’t 
remember until now.

00:19:45.880 --> 00:19:48.840
Because I’m also socially awkward.

00:19:49.360 --> 00:19:51.310
I end my turn.

00:19:51.810 --> 00:19:53.960
My turn.  I draw.

00:19:55.000 --> 00:20:00.250
From my hand, I activate the 
spell card, Gravity Balance.

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:04.050
I select two copies of an 
Earth monster in my graveyard.

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:08.260
By negating ther effects and 
lowering their ATK and DEF to 0...

00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:10.460
...I Special Summon them in defense position.

00:20:11.080 --> 00:20:16.470
I awaken two G Golem Rock Hammers!

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:23.620
Appear!  The circuit that roars the land!

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:28.030
The summoning conditions are two Cyberses.

00:20:28.030 --> 00:20:33.280
I set two G Golem Rock 
Hammers in the Link Markers!

00:20:34.550 --> 00:20:36.020
Link Summon!

00:20:36.520 --> 00:20:38.720
Appear, Link 2!

00:20:43.120 --> 00:20:46.090
G Golem Crystal Heart!

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:26.810
This isn’t a monster effect.

00:21:33.540 --> 00:21:34.780
Oh yeah!

00:21:36.230 --> 00:21:39.960
I remember that monster.

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:41.260
What is it?

00:21:41.260 --> 00:21:43.440
That’s Aqua’s monster.

00:21:43.440 --> 00:21:45.580
Why does Earth have it?

00:21:46.350 --> 00:21:48.600
Aqua’s monster…

00:21:48.600 --> 00:21:55.560
It's time to verify humanity 
and Ai’s future.

00:21:56.770 --> 00:21:58.740
Watch...

00:22:00.580 --> 00:22:02.130
...Aqua.

00:22:19.930 --> 00:22:26.270
Memories that don't disappear
And memories that disappeared

00:22:26.500 --> 00:22:32.970
I quietly "NOW LOADING..." those scenes

00:22:33.400 --> 00:22:36.470
Memories left behind  Erased memories

00:22:36.470 --> 00:22:39.610
What was the PASSWORD again?

00:22:40.040 --> 00:22:44.210
ACCESS records  Restored memories

00:22:44.480 --> 00:22:47.180
Challenge "the you inside you"

00:22:51.890 --> 00:22:58.060
You're a Network  The 
World that spreads beyond

00:22:58.200 --> 00:23:01.200
With repeating "nows"

00:23:01.530 --> 00:23:05.140
What about you?  "Live for now"

00:23:05.300 --> 00:23:11.090
Grab the Shooting Star in 
the sky with both your hands

00:23:11.240 --> 00:23:14.380
Overcome "now" with all your might  Yell!

00:23:36.340 --> 00:23:39.490
The Ignis are AI with free will.

00:23:39.490 --> 00:23:44.400
Their creation made the differences 
between humans and AI fuzzy.

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:46.740
Can they coexist in this world?

00:23:46.740 --> 00:23:50.210
Or will one have to conquer the other?

00:23:50.210 --> 00:23:53.890
To verify which is true, 
Earth continues the duel.

00:23:53.890 --> 00:23:58.750
Cyberse World breaking apart...  
Why do I feel uneasy?

00:23:58.750 --> 00:24:02.640
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
AI's Longing

00:24:02.640 --> 00:24:04.720
Into the VRAINS!
